  "releaseNotes": "PeerSharp 5.2.0 reduces resume persistence and streaming memory use, improves libtorrent compatibility, and fixes hybrid uploads, metadata validation, peer availability, uTP handshakes and UDP tracker disposal. Adds directional MSE policies, BEP 17 HTTP seeds, SSL torrents over TCP/uTP and I2P SAM peer/tracker support. SSL and I2P have local protocol coverage but have not been validated against external SSL peers or a live I2P router. Binary compatible with 5.1.0. See https://github.com/ligenq/PeerSharp/blob/v5.2.0/CHANGELOG.md.",
